# Poly Supermarket 01 - the uFoods interior (docs/SPACEPORT_PLAN.md Phase E, the supply
# run). Bought from Fab, which buys USE and not REDISTRIBUTION, and this repo is public.
# Same rule as every other pack above: bytes stay local, re-install via Fab -> Add to
# Project on a fresh clone.
#
# It will reach the shipped pak through DirectoriesToAlwaysCook in DefaultGame.ini once
# L_uFoods actually uses it - Meshes and Materials, NOT Levels: the pack's L_Showcase and
# L_Overview are layout reference for building the interior, never something a player
# loads. That is exactly how the Rocket_Launch_Pad pack is handled.
Content/Poly_Supermarket_01/

# Build, package and commandlet logs written to the REPO ROOT by Tools/Scripts.
# Root-level only (/*.log), so nothing under Saved/ or Content/ is affected.
#
# 83 of these were already tracked when this rule was added (build-*.log, gate-*.log,
# pkg-v0*.log and friends) and they STAY tracked - a tracked file beats an ignore rule,
# and rewriting that much history to tidy up would cost more than the mess does. This
# only stops NEW ones being added.
#
# build-diag.log was untracked at the same time because it is the one that gets
# regenerated, so it showed as modified forever and hid real changes in git status.
/*.log

# ---- Elite Landscapes: Alien Part IV (Velarion, bought 2026-09-04) -----------
# Purchased vendor pack, 3.2 GB, and this repo is PUBLIC. It was NOT ignored on
# arrival - the same near-miss as Poly_Supermarket_01, which was one commit away
# from publishing a pack somebody paid for. Ignored before anything was staged.
#
# Six 8K landscape maps ship in it; docs/SEVENTH_POWER.md rev 3 wants exactly ONE
# for Grok. Only that map gets a +MapsToCook line, so the cooker follows only its
# references and the other five landscapes never reach the pak. A level hard-
# references what it places, so this needs no DirectoriesToAlwaysCook rule - the
# L_uFoods arrangement, not the Rocket_Launch_Pad one.
Content/Elite_AlienPack_04/

# ---- L_Grok: a 647 MB copy of purchased terrain -----------------------------
# A LANDSCAPE LIVES INSIDE ITS .umap. L_Grok is duplicated from Elite Landscapes:
# Alien Part IV, so this file IS Velarion's heightmap and weightmap data under a
# different name - not a reference to it, the way L_uFoods merely references the
# supermarket's meshes. Committing it to a PUBLIC repo republishes a pack somebody
# has to pay for, which is what ignoring Content/Elite_AlienPack_04/ was for.
#
# THE COST OF THIS LINE: the level is not backed up and not reproducible from a
# clean clone. The answer is the pattern this repo already uses everywhere else -
# Tools/Scripts/make_grok_from_alien.py rebuilds it from the pack, and anything
# placed on it (Nyra, her stage-4 trigger) should be placed BY A SCRIPT that is
# committed, exactly as place_supply_counter.py and place_spaceport_lawn_marker.py
# do. Then the repo holds the recipe and never the vendor's bytes.
#
# If Walt decides the licence permits it, or the repo goes private, delete this.
Content/Maps/L_Grok.umap
Content/ElvenArchitecture/
Content/Maps/L_SibeliusHotel.umap
Content/Maps/L_SibeliusHotel_Generated.umap

# ---- Portal and SavePoint VFX (Dr.Game, bought 2026-09-05) -------------------
# 142 MB purchased vendor pack, public repo. Third one this week to arrive NOT
# ignored; the ritual is now: buy, add, ignore, THEN touch anything else.
#
# 14 Niagara systems with exposed override parameters, which is what makes them
# usable from C++ without authoring a node graph. They reach the pak by HARD
# reference from AWormholeArrival's constructor (FObjectFinder) - a soft path
# alone is the v0.7.4 miss that shipped an invisible spaceport, and a portal
# that works in PIE and is missing from the build would be that bug again in
# the last scene of the game.
Content/PortalVFX/

# ---- Retro Pinball Machines (Speedbump Games, bought 2026-09-27) ---------------
# $6.99, Fab Standard License, public repo. Arrived NOT ignored, like PortalVFX
# before it; caught by `git status` before anything was committed.
#
# Two 1960s-70s electromechanical cabinets (Road Rally, Singalong), UE 5.5-5.8,
# "Generated with AI: No" - so it adds nothing to the Steam AI disclosure. It is
# the SHELL for the living-room table: the ball, flippers and bumpers are drawn by
# the table actor from FPinballSim's layout. Each mesh has its own M_Flipper slot,
# which is how the modelled static flippers get hidden under ours.
#
# When the table actor references the cabinet, make it a HARD reference
# (FObjectFinder), not a soft path - the v0.7.4 invisible-spaceport lesson.
Content/SBG_RetroArcade/
# Its demo level is World Partition, so every actor in it is a separate file under
# these two folders - 146 of them. Same treatment as RestaurantScene and Phantom.
Content/__ExternalActors__/SBG_RetroArcade/
Content/__ExternalObjects__/SBG_RetroArcade/

# --- PijayArt "Classic Billiards Table" (Fab, 2026-09-27, "Generated with AI: No") ---
# The pool table for the living room. Unpacked from the listing's Additional Files
# (the UE 4.20 project), because Fab's in-editor import used the converted glTF, which
# fuses all 19 pieces into one mesh - that copy sits under Content/Fab/, already
# ignored. This one keeps each ball, the cue and the rack as its own mesh, which the
# billiards sim needs. The asset paths are /Game/Billiard_Table/..., so it must live
# at exactly this folder or its material references break.
Content/Billiard_Table/

# --- PixelForgeESP "Interior Essentials: Retro Bowling Alley" (Fab, 2026-09-27, "Generated with AI: No") ---
# The room for the bowling alley, reached by a door in the living room. Paid pack: never in
# the public repo. Its levels are not World Partition (no __ExternalActors__ folder), but
# ignore those paths too in case a copy of its map is ever converted.
Content/IE_RetroBowl/
Content/__ExternalActors__/IE_RetroBowl/
Content/__ExternalObjects__/IE_RetroBowl/
# L_Bowling is the pack's own L_Map, saved as a copy: publishing it would publish the pack's
# level design, so it stays local (backed up to E:), like the pinball pack's demo level. How
# it was set up is written down in BowlingLane.h, so it can be rebuilt from the pack. The pin,
# its materials and the door sign in this folder are ours, and ARE tracked.
Content/Bowling/L_Bowling.umap
Content/Bowling/*_BuiltData.uasset

# --- Tomas Dvorak "Chess Set" (Fab, free, Standard License, 2026-09-28, "Generated with AI: No") ---
# The board and 32 separate pieces for the park chess table in Transhuman City, imported from
# the listing's FBX download. A vendor asset: never in the public repo, even free. The raw
# download (FBX + PNGs) sits unpacked in Tools/VendorSource/ for Tools/Scripts/import_chess_set.py.
Content/ChessSet/
Tools/VendorSource/

# The UnrealClaude editor plugin writes every script Claude runs in the editor here. Scratch,
# not project content.
Content/UnrealClaude/

